Product Requirement Document: Personal Finance & Expense Manager
1. Executive Summary
Objective: To provide a secure and intuitive platform for individuals to monitor their spending habits, manage monthly budgets, and gain clear insights into their financial health through automated data visualization.

2. Target Audience
Individual Users: People looking to move away from manual spreadsheets to a more automated, accessible financial tracking solution.

Budget-Conscious Professionals: Users who need to categorize expenses to identify potential savings.

3. Core Features & Functional Requirements
3.1 Secure User Onboarding
Personalized Accounts: Users must be able to create an account and log in securely to keep their financial data private.

Session Security: The system must ensure that users remain logged in during their session but are prompted to re-authenticate after periods of inactivity.

3.2 Transaction Management
Expense Logging: Users can record new expenses by inputting the amount, selecting a date, and adding a brief description.

Categorization: Every expense must be assigned a category (e.g., Groceries, Utilities, Transport, Entertainment) to allow for organized reporting.

History Log: A searchable and filterable list of all past transactions, allowing users to review or modify previous entries.

3.3 Financial Health Dashboard
Spending Overview: A central hub showing the total amount spent within the current calendar month.

Visual Analytics: Real-time charts that break down spending by category, helping users identify where most of their money is going at a glance.

Historical Trends: A comparative view of spending patterns over previous months.

3.4 Budgeting Tools
Limit Setting: Users can set a target maximum spend for the month.

Progress Tracking: Visual indicators (such as progress bars) that show how much of the monthly budget remains.

Threshold Alerts: The system should visually flag when a user is nearing or has exceeded their set budget.

4. User Experience & Design Goals
Simplicity First: The interface should minimize the number of clicks required to add an expense.

Mobile-Friendly: The application must be fully functional on mobile devices for "on-the-go" logging.

Immediate Feedback: Whenever a user adds or deletes an expense, the dashboard and charts should update instantly to reflect the new balance.

5. Success Metrics
Engagement: Users logging at least 5 transactions per week.

Retention: Users returning month-over-month to set new budget goals.

Accuracy: Zero discrepancy between individual logged items and the total displayed on the dashboard.